  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is placed on a plank of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi><mo>,</mo></math> which is placed on a smooth horizontal plane, as shown in the figure. The coefficient of friction between the block and the plank is <math><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> . If a horizontal force <math><mi>F</mi></math> is applied on the plank, then the maximum value of <math><mi>F</mi></math> for which the block and the plank move together is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0110_3793344bdda2.jpg\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 67px;\" />"
  },
